meta {
  name: 6b. Verify Login PIN
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/verify-pin
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "transactionPin": "1234"
  }
}

docs {
  # Verify Login PIN

  Use this when the app wants to confirm that the user's 4-digit PIN is correct.

  ## Endpoint

  `POST /api/v1/auth/verify-pin`

  ## Authentication

  Required.

  ```txt
  Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
  ```

  ## Body Fields

  `transactionPin`
  Required. The user's 4-digit PIN.

  ## Expected Success Response

  ```json
  {
    "message": "PIN verified successfully",
    "pinVerified": true
  }
  ```

  ## Frontend Notes

  This endpoint is useful when enabling local PIN/biometric unlock or before sensitive wallet actions.

  Do not send fingerprint or Face ID data to the backend. Biometric verification happens inside the mobile device.
}
